1
00:00:04,240 --> 00:00:06,320
They totally won that round!

2
00:00:06,620 --> 00:00:08,240
Now I've been Bucksnapped!

3
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:12,517
I figured Sol Ream would whip out
a teleportation circle, but still,

4
00:00:12,600 --> 00:00:16,306
this is my second time as a
pilfered purveyor of vending goods!

5
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:19,200
Sorry things had to turn
out this way, Boxxo.

6
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:22,980
Not to interrupt, but where am I?

7
00:00:23,560 --> 00:00:26,177
Pity was in the effect
radius and got gotted.

8
00:00:26,260 --> 00:00:28,320
She's been through shell and back.

9
00:00:37,060 --> 00:00:41,697
On the outside, I'm just a big metal box,
but inside, I've still got a human soul!

10
00:00:41,780 --> 00:00:43,237
In this new world of wonders,

11
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:46,817
I travel to and fro on the back
of my super strong partner, Lamas!

12
00:00:46,900 --> 00:00:48,900
The name's Box Up! Hello there!

13
00:00:49,140 --> 00:00:50,728
That means yes, by the way!

14
00:01:00,920 --> 00:01:01,777
Potassium.

15
00:01:01,860 --> 00:01:03,617
Digital. O?

16
00:01:03,700 --> 00:01:05,920
Have you told me?

17
00:01:06,200 --> 00:01:11,820
Can we feel like a father's
dream in this dream?

18
00:01:19,460 --> 00:01:20,860
Oh

19
00:01:59,560 --> 00:02:03,325
This dungeon stratum houses the
Netherlord's base of operations.

20
00:02:03,820 --> 00:02:04,660
No way!

21
00:02:04,940 --> 00:02:06,537
The Netherlord's around these parts?

22
00:02:06,620 --> 00:02:09,537
Feels like I cheat-coded
my way to the final boss.

23
00:02:09,620 --> 00:02:12,897
We've been trying to clear this
stratum since we made our agreement,

24
00:02:12,980 --> 00:02:15,686
but we're sorely lacking
in food and supplies.

25
00:02:16,320 --> 00:02:19,497
It's painfully obvious that
we desperately need your help.

26
00:02:19,580 --> 00:02:22,639
Pretending we were after
pity was an elaborate ruse.

27
00:02:22,740 --> 00:02:26,317
Thing is, you're the one we've
been waiting for this whole time.

28
00:02:26,400 --> 00:02:27,957
Pity is just...

29
00:02:28,040 --> 00:02:29,060
bycatch?

30
00:02:29,800 --> 00:02:32,271
I realize it's useless to haggle with you,

31
00:02:32,400 --> 00:02:36,380
so just be a sport and agree to
go exploring with us. Please?

32
00:02:36,920 --> 00:02:37,780
Too bad!

33
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:39,920
Sure I can't tempt you?

34
00:02:40,520 --> 00:02:41,440
Too bad.

35
00:02:42,060 --> 00:02:45,237
I know the whole cursed kid
sitch is a heavy load to bear,

36
00:02:45,320 --> 00:02:48,849
but I refuse to plop out a cold
can of betrayal for my pals.

37
00:02:49,380 --> 00:02:50,210
Understood.

38
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:53,460
Well, I had a feeling you'd say that.

39
00:02:54,960 --> 00:02:55,790
And you?

40
00:02:56,100 --> 00:02:58,276
Want to team up with the fools again?

41
00:02:58,660 --> 00:02:59,760
Pity can't do it.

42
00:03:00,220 --> 00:03:03,044
I'm already helping Heavy
and all of the others.

43
00:03:03,200 --> 00:03:04,500
I made a promise.

44
00:03:05,280 --> 00:03:09,000
Even if I agree to grant you any
wish a little clan could want?

45
00:03:09,280 --> 00:03:12,737
Such as reclaiming the heart
of the man you loved and lost?

46
00:03:12,820 --> 00:03:15,017
All he's missing are
horns and a pitchfork!

47
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:16,140
I can't... Huh?

48
00:03:16,960 --> 00:03:19,489
This is something I've
got to do on my own.

49
00:03:20,160 --> 00:03:20,990
Somehow.

50
00:03:21,480 --> 00:03:23,480
I'll find a way to bring him back.

51
00:03:23,660 --> 00:03:25,240
So the answer's no.

52
00:03:25,980 --> 00:03:26,810
Go, pity!

53
00:03:26,960 --> 00:03:28,019
Her defense is OP!

54
00:03:28,240 --> 00:03:30,917
And her heart is clearly
too pure for this world.

55
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:34,176
Why must I be so stubborn
about anything love-related?

56
00:03:34,540 --> 00:03:36,800
Luckily for you, I'm a patient man.

57
00:03:37,240 --> 00:03:40,828
I'm not going to let you out,
not until you agree to join us.

58
00:03:41,800 --> 00:03:43,220
Give me the goods, Boxo!

59
00:03:43,380 --> 00:03:45,637
I've got a mad craving for
that fried meat of yours!

60
00:03:45,720 --> 00:03:46,661
I want some too!

61
00:03:46,920 --> 00:03:49,449
They may suck, but
they're still customers.

62
00:03:49,740 --> 00:03:50,570
What to do?

63
00:03:50,740 --> 00:03:52,681
Just giving in sounds hella lame.

64
00:03:55,380 --> 00:03:58,857
Hey, what's the big idea of replacing the
fizzy - Wait, you put her on that one!

65
00:03:58,940 --> 00:04:00,917
We know you've got meats
and sweets in there!

66
00:04:01,000 --> 00:04:02,260
If you insist.

67
00:04:03,640 --> 00:04:04,640
Hello there.

68
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:07,417
Thanks, I knew you
wouldn't do us like that.

69
00:04:07,500 --> 00:04:09,197
I wonder what I should order first.

70
00:04:09,280 --> 00:04:10,110
Those prices!

71
00:04:10,193 --> 00:04:12,314
Hey, that's ten times as much as usual!

72
00:04:12,520 --> 00:04:13,350
Booyah!

73
00:04:13,433 --> 00:04:16,837
Us humble vending machines always
charge more at destination spots,

74
00:04:16,920 --> 00:04:18,160
like enemy lairs.

75
00:04:18,480 --> 00:04:20,020
Please insert coins.

76
00:04:20,500 --> 00:04:22,357
It's extortion or blackmail or something!

77
00:04:22,440 --> 00:04:24,499
I don't wanna pay, but I'm gonna...

78
00:04:26,220 --> 00:04:28,780
Uh-oh. Emergency. No toilet.

79
00:04:29,660 --> 00:04:31,037
You, Pa-Octa-E.

80
00:04:31,120 --> 00:04:33,820
It's pity, remember?

81
00:04:45,520 --> 00:04:47,140
Thanks a bunch.

82
00:04:55,540 --> 00:04:57,700
It's so soft.

83
00:04:58,640 --> 00:05:01,677
you're really the best and so kind to me

84
00:05:01,760 --> 00:05:08,397
it's time to rise and
shine are you kidding

85
00:05:08,480 --> 00:05:12,057
me with this what's wrong did something

86
00:05:12,140 --> 00:05:17,657
bad happen oh my goodness wow how lovely

87
00:05:17,740 --> 00:05:23,437
it's a shame i'll have to leave one day
you're not taking this whole prisoner

88
00:05:23,520 --> 00:05:29,040
thing seriously prison schmizzen it's My
duty as a vending machine to dispense joy.

89
00:05:29,480 --> 00:05:32,080
I assume you both reconsidered my offer?

90
00:05:32,680 --> 00:05:33,700
It's still a no.

91
00:05:34,400 --> 00:05:35,540
Ever, ever.

92
00:05:36,160 --> 00:05:38,397
That didn't exactly sound like a chipper.

93
00:05:38,480 --> 00:05:42,009
Hello there, so I guess that
means I should take it as a no.

94
00:05:42,780 --> 00:05:45,240
Come on, must we play these silly games?

95
00:05:45,720 --> 00:05:48,661
You realize I'm giving you
the good cop treatment.

96
00:05:48,800 --> 00:05:51,741
You won't get that from
Sulreeman, the Netherlord.

97
00:05:52,120 --> 00:05:54,757
Soon you'll just be a pile
of parts and clan chowder.

98
00:05:54,840 --> 00:05:57,500
I'd say you probably have one week max

99
00:05:58,120 --> 00:05:58,950
Got it?

100
00:05:59,160 --> 00:06:00,377
Just one week left.

101
00:06:00,460 --> 00:06:02,300
Don't let it slip away.

102
00:06:04,620 --> 00:06:06,697
I think he was trying to help us.

103
00:06:06,780 --> 00:06:08,677
We've got to escape.

104
00:06:08,760 --> 00:06:10,337
Within one week?

105
00:06:10,420 --> 00:06:11,500
Yes!

106
00:06:13,300 --> 00:06:15,257
Hey, Voxo, help me out?

107
00:06:15,340 --> 00:06:16,937
I need another hint of food!

108
00:06:17,020 --> 00:06:17,850
It's busy.

109
00:06:17,933 --> 00:06:18,797
This broke is a joke.

110
00:06:18,880 --> 00:06:20,440
Have some mercy, will ya?

111
00:06:20,820 --> 00:06:24,037
That's just sad You want Voxo?

112
00:06:24,120 --> 00:06:26,020
I'm going to destroy myself.

113
00:06:27,020 --> 00:06:29,491
Must be hard to get good grub around here.

114
00:06:32,440 --> 00:06:33,381
What's he doing?

115
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:34,980
It's for you.

116
00:06:35,340 --> 00:06:36,177
Whoa, if we be.

117
00:06:36,260 --> 00:06:39,260
You're the best magic item
with consciousness ever.

118
00:06:39,980 --> 00:06:41,440
Listen up, Boxman.

119
00:06:41,780 --> 00:06:43,240
I got something to say.

120
00:06:43,600 --> 00:06:45,620
We really love our old buddies.

121
00:06:45,860 --> 00:06:48,177
I know that sounds hard
to believe, but it's true.

122
00:06:48,260 --> 00:06:50,140
We love you guys like crazy.

123
00:06:50,480 --> 00:06:51,951
He's breaking our hearts.

124
00:06:53,140 --> 00:06:57,100
So Shiro's a clingy drunk and
Akka's a weepy drunk. Pretty cringe.

125
00:06:58,420 --> 00:07:00,897
Well, let's see what kind
of deets they let slip.

126
00:07:00,980 --> 00:07:02,720
I got more to tell you.

127
00:07:03,120 --> 00:07:05,700
They're these stupid five-figure generals.

128
00:07:05,900 --> 00:07:08,724
Those assholes think
they're so fucking special.

129
00:07:09,220 --> 00:07:10,161
Freeze, brother.

130
00:07:10,400 --> 00:07:11,677
It's not that I'm complaining,

131
00:07:11,760 --> 00:07:15,377
but I haven't seen the nether lord
or most of the generals in ages.

132
00:07:15,460 --> 00:07:18,620
The pinky finger along
with the index finger.

133
00:07:18,760 --> 00:07:20,936
Oh, and the thumb finger are missing.

134
00:07:21,300 --> 00:07:23,418
I wonder what those jerks are doing.

135
00:07:23,880 --> 00:07:27,233
We captured the Pinky General
in the Dark Forest Stratum.

136
00:07:27,760 --> 00:07:29,540
Bet Solream's the Ring-Fingy.

137
00:07:30,220 --> 00:07:32,877
If the Index and the Thumb
Generals are M .I .A.,

138
00:07:32,960 --> 00:07:35,372
the Middle Fingy's around here somewhere.

139
00:07:36,300 --> 00:07:37,130
In-E!

140
00:07:38,040 --> 00:07:38,870
Sir!

141
00:07:39,020 --> 00:07:40,760
There are a ton of monsters.

142
00:07:41,000 --> 00:07:43,377
To make it worse, their
grunts are all Skellington,

143
00:07:43,460 --> 00:07:45,519
so it's creepy as heck around here.

144
00:07:45,660 --> 00:07:48,248
So many, I'd say there's
at least a hundred.

145
00:07:50,460 --> 00:07:52,937
The Skellingtons won't even
make polite conversation.

146
00:07:53,020 --> 00:07:55,740
It's so rude and majorly
hurts my feelings.

147
00:07:56,320 --> 00:07:58,057
Oh, and they've got human jerks, too,

148
00:07:58,140 --> 00:08:01,552
wearing these creepy coats
that aren't even a little cool.

149
00:08:01,840 --> 00:08:04,958
We don't know if they're
humans or just look like it.

150
00:08:05,480 --> 00:08:07,951
I kind of want one of those coats, though.

151
00:08:10,180 --> 00:08:13,062
They're asleep, and they
left the door wide open.

152
00:08:13,320 --> 00:08:14,732
There you are, children.

153
00:08:14,840 --> 00:08:16,180
This won't do at all.

154
00:08:19,760 --> 00:08:22,231
We'll discuss your drinking problem later.

155
00:08:23,180 --> 00:08:24,160
Hello, Boxo.

156
00:08:24,480 --> 00:08:26,757
Lady Sulream would like to speak with you.

157
00:08:26,840 --> 00:08:28,020
Please accompany me.

158
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:30,321
I'm afraid pity must stay behind.

159
00:08:31,400 --> 00:08:33,020
Put your backs into it.

160
00:08:33,880 --> 00:08:34,720
Jeez, brutal.

161
00:08:34,900 --> 00:08:36,977
Hummus must be even
stronger than I thought.

162
00:08:37,060 --> 00:08:38,240
Isn't Boxo heavy?

163
00:08:38,720 --> 00:08:40,597
I don't have the build for this.

164
00:08:40,680 --> 00:08:45,209
I could transform into my cardboard
self, but that would be far less amusing.

165
00:08:45,740 --> 00:08:47,505
You reap what you sow, kiddos.

166
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:54,020
Lady Sulream, we brought
you Boxxo as requested.

167
00:08:54,400 --> 00:08:55,660
A job well done.

168
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:58,941
Now leave that thing here
and get out of my sight.

169
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:00,300
Yes, of course.

170
00:09:00,940 --> 00:09:02,200
Whatever you say.

171
00:09:02,960 --> 00:09:04,640
Please, stay on your guard.

172
00:09:07,240 --> 00:09:09,760
Boxxo, I hear you're a sapient magic item.

173
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:13,720
I may despise humans, but I'm
fine with sentient conveniences.

174
00:09:14,080 --> 00:09:17,315
Though I'll still destroy
you if you seek to oppose me.

175
00:09:17,540 --> 00:09:18,380
That's weird.

176
00:09:18,700 --> 00:09:20,077
Where's the captain's son?

177
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:21,857
I thought the big bummer
about the blessing of

178
00:09:21,940 --> 00:09:24,297
decay was that it only
stops if she's near him.

179
00:09:24,380 --> 00:09:25,317
Big Sis, where are you?

180
00:09:25,400 --> 00:09:26,230
There he is.

181
00:09:26,640 --> 00:09:29,617
Goodness, your hair's sopping
wet and dripping everywhere.

182
00:09:29,700 --> 00:09:30,540
Such a mess.

183
00:09:30,780 --> 00:09:31,757
Come let me try it.

184
00:09:31,840 --> 00:09:32,670
Thanks.

185
00:09:32,753 --> 00:09:33,771
You're the best, Big Sis.

186
00:09:34,000 --> 00:09:35,060
Big what now?

187
00:09:35,300 --> 00:09:37,771
I'm sorry for pushing you so hard earlier.

188
00:09:37,880 --> 00:09:39,115
You sure you're okay?

189
00:09:39,640 --> 00:09:41,040
Not a scratch on me.

190
00:09:41,500 --> 00:09:44,077
Did I do a good job
pretending to be tortured?

191
00:09:44,160 --> 00:09:44,990
It was perfect.

192
00:09:45,073 --> 00:09:47,178
You're such a talented little actor.

193
00:09:48,180 --> 00:09:49,010
Actor?

194
00:09:49,093 --> 00:09:52,425
Meaning the munchkin went method
and had us totally marking out.

195
00:09:52,740 --> 00:09:55,320
Now then, be careful
not to wander too far.

196
00:09:55,540 --> 00:09:58,717
I won't be able to keep your
negative blessing at bay if you do.

197
00:09:58,800 --> 00:10:00,760
I promise. I'll be careful.

198
00:10:01,540 --> 00:10:02,370
Weird.

199
00:10:02,453 --> 00:10:04,617
It's like watching a
family from an old sitcom.

200
00:10:04,700 --> 00:10:06,040
I am so confused.

201
00:10:06,400 --> 00:10:07,620
Hey, big sis!

202
00:10:07,960 --> 00:10:09,537
Is that the talking box thing?

203
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:10,860
Yes, that's the one.

204
00:10:11,080 --> 00:10:13,797
You said you wanted to
see it, and so here it is.

205
00:10:13,880 --> 00:10:14,977
Go and give it a try.

206
00:10:15,060 --> 00:10:17,200
Isn't it actually a real person?

207
00:10:17,720 --> 00:10:21,297
And doesn't that mean we're not supposed
to let it see us stop pretending?

208
00:10:21,380 --> 00:10:22,615
Don't worry yourself.

209
00:10:23,000 --> 00:10:25,059
It has a rather limited vocabulary.

210
00:10:25,240 --> 00:10:28,475
And there's no one here it
can speak to telepathically.

211
00:10:29,100 --> 00:10:29,930
Hello there.

212
00:10:30,160 --> 00:10:31,620
Wow, it really talks.

213
00:10:31,840 --> 00:10:34,197
Do you think it would be okay
if I bought something from it?

214
00:10:34,280 --> 00:10:35,460
Of course it would.

215
00:10:35,640 --> 00:10:37,037
Buy whatever you please.

216
00:10:37,120 --> 00:10:38,480
Please insert coins.

217
00:10:38,920 --> 00:10:40,038
I don't have money.

218
00:10:41,140 --> 00:10:42,797
Here, buy as much as you want.

219
00:10:42,880 --> 00:10:43,710
It's my treat.

220
00:10:43,793 --> 00:10:45,880
She is spoiling the kid rotten.

221
00:10:47,440 --> 00:10:50,640
I've never seen so many
weird-looking drinks.

222
00:10:51,220 --> 00:10:53,980
Eeny, meeny, miny, moe!

223
00:10:54,640 --> 00:10:56,875
That expression is all kinds of wrong.

224
00:10:57,020 --> 00:10:58,785
Which drink are you gonna get?

225
00:10:59,540 --> 00:11:01,400
Oh, I'd be happy with anything.

226
00:11:01,740 --> 00:11:03,157
Why don't you pick for me?

227
00:11:03,240 --> 00:11:06,160
I've already gotten
everything I ever dreamed of.

228
00:11:06,380 --> 00:11:07,700
Slee, child!

229
00:11:08,140 --> 00:11:10,420
We call this shiz stranger danger!

230
00:11:10,700 --> 00:11:12,097
That chick belongs on a registry.

231
00:11:12,180 --> 00:11:15,257
This poor kid got curse whammy, then
woke up only to be held hostage.

232
00:11:15,340 --> 00:11:17,417
It's like a Russian novel anime style.

233
00:11:17,500 --> 00:11:21,500
Wait, why does he seem to respect
that walking after-school special?

234
00:11:21,860 --> 00:11:23,360
Uh... Oh! Lifeline!

235
00:11:23,580 --> 00:11:26,517
Since snow people are children
until they suddenly become adults,

236
00:11:26,600 --> 00:11:28,437
maybe the ick factor is reduced?

237
00:11:28,520 --> 00:11:31,040
I did not just think that! This is whack!

238
00:11:31,680 --> 00:11:32,510
Lamas!

239
00:11:32,593 --> 00:11:33,423
Save me!

240
00:11:35,140 --> 00:11:36,757
Sorry, I'd love to keep playing,

241
00:11:36,840 --> 00:11:41,257
but I need to take a teensy nap after
using so much stamina on teleportation.

242
00:11:41,340 --> 00:11:43,417
I'm afraid I haven't fully recovered yet.

243
00:11:43,500 --> 00:11:46,697
Okay, have a nice nap, but, um...

244
00:11:46,780 --> 00:11:50,780
Can I have permission to buy more
stuff from Boxo while you're away?

245
00:11:50,960 --> 00:11:52,100
Of course you can.

246
00:11:52,220 --> 00:11:53,257
Buy whatever you want.

247
00:11:53,340 --> 00:11:55,597
Just be sure to brush your
teeth if you have any sweets.

248
00:11:55,680 --> 00:11:56,510
Promise!

249
00:11:59,420 --> 00:12:00,250
We're alone.

250
00:12:00,460 --> 00:12:01,931
I need to speak with you.

251
00:12:02,720 --> 00:12:06,500
I act that way to fool her, by
exaggerating my youthfulness.

252
00:12:07,260 --> 00:12:08,760
Sorry I was deceptive.

253
00:12:08,900 --> 00:12:10,194
You deserve the truth.

254
00:12:10,400 --> 00:12:11,230
Huh?

255
00:12:11,313 --> 00:12:13,437
I know I caused my family much suffering,

256
00:12:13,520 --> 00:12:15,797
and it weighs on me more
than you could know.

257
00:12:15,880 --> 00:12:16,939
I'm such a burden.

258
00:12:17,260 --> 00:12:19,397
The world would be much
better off without me.

259
00:12:19,480 --> 00:12:22,797
But I won't waste a life they
sacrificed so much to save.

260
00:12:22,880 --> 00:12:26,762
That would be a disservice to them,
and I simply couldn't bear it.

261
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:32,337
I'm masquerading as an obedient kid
to gather intel on their inner circle.

262
00:12:32,420 --> 00:12:36,380
As for the curse, it truly pains
me to deceive my own family.

263
00:12:36,660 --> 00:12:39,037
But my little bros are
bad at keeping secrets.

264
00:12:39,120 --> 00:12:41,620
He looks like a child, but when he speaks,

265
00:12:41,720 --> 00:12:44,657
it's pretty dang clear he's
older than those immature twins.

266
00:12:44,740 --> 00:12:46,700
I know you have wondrous powers.

267
00:12:47,060 --> 00:12:49,937
My parents told me everything
about you and your gifts.

268
00:12:50,020 --> 00:12:52,197
They want you to stay here and serve them.

269
00:12:52,280 --> 00:12:53,809
Refusal means destruction.

270
00:12:54,260 --> 00:12:55,090
Yes.

271
00:12:55,173 --> 00:12:56,962
Do you have any means of escape?

272
00:12:57,260 --> 00:13:00,737
I'll gladly do anything in my
power to help you pull it off.

273
00:13:00,820 --> 00:13:01,657
Think it through.

274
00:13:01,740 --> 00:13:02,916
There must be a way.

275
00:13:04,480 --> 00:13:08,177
The next few days, I spent my
mornings vending Pity's breakfast.

276
00:13:08,260 --> 00:13:12,142
After that, I was whisked away to
Solream's pad to then some more.

277
00:13:12,560 --> 00:13:15,297
After Brekkie, but before
lunch, so technically brunch,

278
00:13:15,380 --> 00:13:18,792
I was wheeled to a cafeteria
with humans and beast people.

279
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:22,820
Look who it is.

280
00:13:23,640 --> 00:13:24,600
I'm back.

281
00:13:25,500 --> 00:13:26,677
You're early today.

282
00:13:26,760 --> 00:13:27,995
What a nice surprise.

283
00:13:28,700 --> 00:13:32,280
By the way, I wouldn't
say no to more food.

284
00:13:34,780 --> 00:13:37,960
For today, will you stay with me?

285
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:39,690
Yes!

286
00:13:40,020 --> 00:13:41,220
That makes me happy.

287
00:13:44,740 --> 00:13:47,480
Is pity crushing on a
certain vending machine?

288
00:13:47,820 --> 00:13:51,240
Like always, your food is delicious.

289
00:13:52,400 --> 00:13:54,520
Thanks, Poxo. Say what?

290
00:13:54,740 --> 00:13:57,437
Me thinks that's the first time
she's called me by my name.

291
00:13:57,520 --> 00:14:00,417
Is this that suspension bridge
effect thingy from psychology?

292
00:14:00,500 --> 00:14:03,897
When in imminent danger you mistake
the pounding of your heart for lust?

293
00:14:03,980 --> 00:14:06,840
I swear it's just psychology, Lamas!

294
00:14:08,560 --> 00:14:09,913
Psychology doesn't lie!

295
00:14:10,020 --> 00:14:11,060
Please, Lamas!

296
00:14:13,600 --> 00:14:15,437
I hope you're properly prepared.

297
00:14:15,520 --> 00:14:16,873
Tomorrow's the big day.

298
00:14:17,200 --> 00:14:18,030
Hello there!

299
00:14:18,520 --> 00:14:21,097
Oh man, I almost forgot
that was even happening.

300
00:14:21,180 --> 00:14:22,737
The catered meeting on the roof.

301
00:14:22,820 --> 00:14:24,080
It's not fair, Akka.

302
00:14:24,280 --> 00:14:28,060
Only our Big Bro, Boxo, Pitty,
and Sulream are invited to go.

303
00:14:29,220 --> 00:14:30,050
Yep.

304
00:14:30,133 --> 00:14:31,917
Solream's trying to pass it
off as a catered meeting,

305
00:14:32,000 --> 00:14:34,317
but it's really just a
rooftop barbecue party.

306
00:14:34,400 --> 00:14:36,077
All because...

307
00:14:36,160 --> 00:14:40,260
Big Sis, I really, really, really
want to eat outside tomorrow.

308
00:14:40,540 --> 00:14:42,237
I know it's against the rules.

309
00:14:42,320 --> 00:14:44,202
Can I do it on the roof instead?

310
00:14:44,900 --> 00:14:47,757
Sulream was powerless
against his S-rank cuteness.

311
00:14:47,840 --> 00:14:48,720
No comment.

312
00:14:49,400 --> 00:14:51,657
He even convinced her
to invite pity so she

313
00:14:51,740 --> 00:14:54,622
could use her blessing of
weight to get me there.

314
00:14:54,900 --> 00:14:57,597
It's the perfect chance
to escape their fortress.

315
00:14:57,680 --> 00:15:01,100
If I botch this, it's probably
curtains for both of us.

316
00:15:01,420 --> 00:15:03,957
It would seem the middle-fingered
general was nearby.

317
00:15:04,040 --> 00:15:06,600
I heard the goons talking about it,

318
00:15:07,040 --> 00:15:09,877
though we've yet to see the
general with their own eyes.

319
00:15:09,960 --> 00:15:11,220
The middle thingy.

320
00:15:11,520 --> 00:15:14,461
Not knowing what to expect
makes me super nervous.

321
00:15:17,120 --> 00:15:18,477
Boxo, don't worry.

322
00:15:18,560 --> 00:15:19,480
You'll see.

323
00:15:19,760 --> 00:15:20,620
We'll be fine.

324
00:15:21,540 --> 00:15:23,077
Oh, I must have been blinking.

325
00:15:23,160 --> 00:15:25,101
I should be vending, not venting.

326
00:15:25,600 --> 00:15:26,900
Thank you very much.

327
00:15:27,800 --> 00:15:28,630
Dammit,

328
00:15:28,713 --> 00:15:31,057
when I think of all the cool
stuff Boxo's about to do,

329
00:15:31,140 --> 00:15:32,964
I want to ditch the netherlord.

330
00:15:33,060 --> 00:15:34,597
Same for me! Team Boxxo!

331
00:15:34,680 --> 00:15:36,197
Team Fried Meat and Fizzies!

332
00:15:36,280 --> 00:15:40,280
Please make sure to get a nice
recording of your reunion with Lamas.

333
00:15:40,880 --> 00:15:43,040
Am I the only normal one here?

334
00:15:50,660 --> 00:15:52,500
Boxxo, no peeking.

335
00:15:53,460 --> 00:15:54,290
Yes!

336
00:15:57,960 --> 00:15:58,940
To business!

337
00:16:12,300 --> 00:16:13,130
Boom!

338
00:16:13,320 --> 00:16:17,732
These coin lockers preserve freshness,
so I'm using them for the big lunch.

339
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:22,320
Petitrusts in Boxo. Completely.

340
00:16:24,280 --> 00:16:26,162
Looks like you're ready to roll.

341
00:16:26,520 --> 00:16:27,620
Well, let's go.

342
00:16:28,500 --> 00:16:33,037
No one's allowed on the roof until lunch,
so you'll be on your own until then.

343
00:16:33,120 --> 00:16:35,296
Surin's orders were incredibly clean.

344
00:16:35,760 --> 00:16:37,100
None shall pass!

345
00:16:37,320 --> 00:16:38,557
Isn't that right, Shiro?

346
00:16:38,640 --> 00:16:41,317
Yeah, not on our watch,
Aka. That's correct.

347
00:16:41,400 --> 00:16:44,397
We have no choice but to
follow the orders given to us.

348
00:16:44,480 --> 00:16:47,277
There's still no sign of
the Middlefinger, General.

349
00:16:47,360 --> 00:16:50,537
True, and I've never seen the
Netherlord here even once.

350
00:16:50,620 --> 00:16:53,855
They're not exactly being
subtle, but that's good info.

351
00:16:57,820 --> 00:16:58,740
See ya.

352
00:16:59,180 --> 00:17:00,100
And take care.

353
00:17:01,300 --> 00:17:02,130
Goodbye.

354
00:17:02,213 --> 00:17:03,526
And thank you for everything.

355
00:17:04,300 --> 00:17:05,600
I mean that.

356
00:17:06,400 --> 00:17:08,660
I look forward to serving you again.

357
00:17:09,260 --> 00:17:10,660
I won't say goodbye.

358
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:12,765
I'm literally incapable of it.

359
00:17:13,640 --> 00:17:16,340
We will meet again. Wait and see.

360
00:17:19,280 --> 00:17:20,420
Here we go.

361
00:17:21,300 --> 00:17:22,980
The guests of honor.

362
00:17:23,540 --> 00:17:24,370
Human,

363
00:17:24,453 --> 00:17:25,737
if you try anything funny,

364
00:17:25,820 --> 00:17:28,897
I'll freeze you on the spot
and keep you as an ice statue.

365
00:17:28,980 --> 00:17:29,810
Noted.

366
00:17:30,320 --> 00:17:31,150
Beautimous.

367
00:17:31,233 --> 00:17:35,274
She thinks I'm a regular old magic
item, so she's only watchdogging pity.

368
00:17:38,360 --> 00:17:39,480
It's so yummy.

369
00:17:39,760 --> 00:17:41,257
You should try it, big sister.

370
00:17:41,340 --> 00:17:43,105
But you already drink from it.

371
00:17:43,360 --> 00:17:46,137
Yeah, I guess you wouldn't want
it after it's been in my mouth.

372
00:17:46,220 --> 00:17:47,577
That is the opposite of the truth.

373
00:17:47,660 --> 00:17:49,660
In fact, it makes me want it more.

374
00:17:52,980 --> 00:17:54,360
Mmm. Score!

375
00:17:54,800 --> 00:17:58,212
That yakiniku sauce has her
slugging them back like crazy.

376
00:17:59,120 --> 00:18:02,217
How come you're wiggling
like that? It's fine.

377
00:18:02,300 --> 00:18:05,160
I just need a little
bathroom break. Go time!

378
00:18:05,520 --> 00:18:07,197
Caffeine has a diuretic effect.

379
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:10,104
You can't chug that much
without nature calling.

380
00:18:10,240 --> 00:18:11,480
I've gotta go, too.

381
00:18:12,500 --> 00:18:14,088
Your name's pity, isn't it?

382
00:18:14,220 --> 00:18:16,457
Don't try anything stupid while I'm gone.

383
00:18:16,540 --> 00:18:18,069
It's impossible to escape.

384
00:18:18,220 --> 00:18:21,237
You're trapped on a rooftop
on an isolated island.

385
00:18:21,320 --> 00:18:23,200
Isn't this fun, Vixis?

386
00:18:23,780 --> 00:18:26,980
Boxxo, please hurry! Yes!

387
00:18:27,840 --> 00:18:29,020
Form change!

388
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:31,500
Balloon vending machine!

389
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:40,740
I'm ready.

390
00:18:41,300 --> 00:18:42,940
I sure hope this works!

391
00:18:43,420 --> 00:18:44,260
Octae?

392
00:18:44,520 --> 00:18:45,420
It's pity!

393
00:18:46,200 --> 00:18:48,300
Actually, I guess that's fine.

394
00:18:49,080 --> 00:18:50,280
Activating it now.

395
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:53,837
Pity's weight blessing is in play.

396
00:18:53,920 --> 00:18:57,214
She made me, herself, and her
shield light as a feather.

397
00:18:57,960 --> 00:18:59,320
House, we did it!

398
00:18:59,540 --> 00:19:01,300
Now for another form change!

399
00:19:01,780 --> 00:19:03,240
Coin-powered vacuum!

400
00:19:04,340 --> 00:19:06,180
I'll bend up some mighty wind.

401
00:19:12,320 --> 00:19:14,280
Hey, Foxo, it's working!

402
00:19:15,440 --> 00:19:17,120
Yes, thank you very much.

403
00:19:20,440 --> 00:19:22,437
The barrier costs a lot of points.

404
00:19:22,520 --> 00:19:23,537
But I've got over a mil!

405
00:19:23,620 --> 00:19:24,577
So it ain't no thing.

406
00:19:24,660 --> 00:19:27,217
We just gotta find an island and...

407
00:19:27,300 --> 00:19:29,517
Boxo, that bin right there?

408
00:19:29,600 --> 00:19:31,740
It seems to be following us!

409
00:19:36,500 --> 00:19:37,560
What's the actual?

410
00:19:37,780 --> 00:19:39,077
It's at least 50 meters.

411
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:40,797
Fly no further!

412
00:19:40,880 --> 00:19:43,097
That bin is telepathic?

413
00:19:43,180 --> 00:19:47,709
You must face punishment and for attempting
to escape the Netherlord's grasp.

414
00:19:47,800 --> 00:19:51,480
As the Middlefinger General,
I will not abide this.

415
00:19:51,860 --> 00:19:53,500
The Middlefingy's a shark?

416
00:19:53,700 --> 00:19:55,057
You don't see that every day.

417
00:19:55,140 --> 00:19:57,117
So that's why he was never at the base.

418
00:19:57,200 --> 00:19:59,540
Take us higher, Balloon Brigade!

419
00:20:00,020 --> 00:20:01,500
There's no escape!

420
00:20:06,180 --> 00:20:08,380
Points reduced by 918.

421
00:20:10,280 --> 00:20:11,480
Happy, happy!

422
00:20:14,720 --> 00:20:17,020
You yellow-bellied coward!

423
00:20:17,580 --> 00:20:20,580
Have you no honor within
that magic box of yours!

424
00:20:21,140 --> 00:20:21,970
Voxo!

425
00:20:22,180 --> 00:20:24,920
He's following us! Crossroads!

426
00:20:25,420 --> 00:20:27,840
Should we try to float away or troll?

427
00:20:31,880 --> 00:20:33,440
Ok, no problem.

428
00:20:33,920 --> 00:20:35,626
I'm guessing you have a plan?

429
00:20:35,900 --> 00:20:36,730
I do!

430
00:20:42,120 --> 00:20:43,540
Form change!

431
00:20:44,580 --> 00:20:46,380
Super-sized vending machine,

432
00:20:46,620 --> 00:20:50,037
complete with the concrete blocks
those big mamas are bolted to.

433
00:20:50,120 --> 00:20:51,720
Ready? Fire!

434
00:20:52,820 --> 00:20:55,720
What the freak is going on here?

435
00:20:56,180 --> 00:20:57,540
You're cucked.

436
00:20:57,700 --> 00:20:58,720
Remove barrier.

437
00:21:01,460 --> 00:21:02,300
Boxo!

438
00:21:02,600 --> 00:21:03,920
Form change!

439
00:21:08,120 --> 00:21:08,960
Nonsense!

440
00:21:09,300 --> 00:21:11,477
Those things appeared as if from nowhere!

441
00:21:11,560 --> 00:21:12,840
Yoo-hoo!

442
00:21:13,300 --> 00:21:15,260
Super-sized Fendi-Machine attack!

443
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:22,270
Fatality.

444
00:21:22,353 --> 00:21:24,497
Now all I got to do is find Pity and...

445
00:21:24,580 --> 00:21:25,410
Huh?

446
00:21:26,800 --> 00:21:28,160
Easier done than said.

447
00:21:28,380 --> 00:21:31,380
Even if she adjusted her
weight, that was reckless.

448
00:21:31,520 --> 00:21:32,360
For Octa-E.

449
00:21:34,000 --> 00:21:35,280
Oh, thank goodness!

450
00:21:36,220 --> 00:21:37,050
You're safe.

451
00:21:38,740 --> 00:21:41,152
That must have been pretty heckin' scary.

452
00:21:41,560 --> 00:21:44,442
This is about the time
Lamas would start yelling.

453
00:21:45,980 --> 00:21:46,810
Legs, huh?

454
00:21:47,000 --> 00:21:49,140
I guess the general was amphibious.

455
00:21:50,000 --> 00:21:52,000
You okay? What's wrong?

456
00:21:52,540 --> 00:21:56,177
I'm getting deja vu from when we
defeated the Netherlord's arm.

457
00:21:56,260 --> 00:21:59,640
If he sees the body, he'll
know this was a boxo joint.

458
00:22:00,160 --> 00:22:03,925
Here's hoping the fishies have
themselves a middle thingy feast.

459
00:22:23,180 --> 00:22:24,580
Oh

460
00:23:01,100 --> 00:23:02,660
I love you?

461
00:23:35,920 --> 00:23:38,040
I look forward to serving you again.
